-- the four mechanisms, as one object. A signal count can differ from another for four reasons, and each
-- is now a refutation about a named compound rather than a distinction drawn in prose. First, a
-- representation that admits permutations no motion performs: the bond graph, wrong for eight of the
-- fourteen compounds in the table. Second, the handedness of the medium: glycerol, whose enantiotopic
-- arms an achiral solvent identifies and a chiral one separates. Third, the rate of a motion against the
-- rate the observation resolves: cyclohexane, one class at room temperature and two at 190 K with
-- nothing about the molecule changed. Fourth, accidental coincidence of shift: leucine, eight classes
-- and seven peaks. The first is a defect in a representation and the other three are not defects at all
-- -- they are what it means for an observation to be of a molecule in a situation. A record that stores
-- a spectrum against a structure can be corrected for the first. It cannot be corrected for the other
-- three without fields for the medium, the temperature and the instrument, which is to say without
-- storing the observation relation rather than the observation.
